      "id": "6accb39f13e0be4f1e5be581",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Brand Awareness Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a brand awareness survey?\", \"a\": \"A brand awareness survey measures how many people in a market know a brand. It asks them to name brands in a category with no hints, then to pick the ones they recognize from a list, and often where they first heard of each one.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you create a brand awareness survey?\", \"a\": \"Open with a screening question for category buyers, then the open recall question, then a shuffled set of brand names that includes your rivals and one made-up name. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> sets up that order from a description, with an answer table behind every round.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some good survey questions to measure brand awareness?\", \"a\": \"Strong brand awareness survey questions run in a fixed order. Ask which brands come to mind in the category, then which listed names people have heard of, then where they first came across yours. How people rate a brand they already know is the job of a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/brand-perception-survey'>brand perception survey</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between aided and unaided questions in a brand awareness survey?\", \"a\": \"Unaided questions give no hints: people name brands from memory. Aided questions show names or logos and ask which ones they know. Recall from memory is the harder test and usually the smaller number. It has to come first, because names seen earlier leak into it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a good length for a brand awareness survey?\", \"a\": \"Four questions carry the study: a screener, open recall, recognition from names shown, and where people first heard of you. Add another only when a decision rests on its answer. Region and age band can come from the screener instead of extra screens at the end.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a brand awareness survey template include?\", \"a\": \"A useful brand awareness survey template holds the screener, the open recall box, a shuffled set of names with one decoy, and the first-heard question, in that order. Describe your category and rivals to Emergent and it builds those screens with a database behind them.\"}, {\"q\": \"Who should you send a brand awareness survey to?\", \"a\": \"Send it to people who buy in your category, customers of yours or not. A sample of customers alone overstates awareness, since every one of them knows the brand. How happy current buyers are is a separate study, a customer satisfaction survey.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can brand awareness surveys track the impact of a campaign?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when you survey before and after it, and in a market the campaign never reached. Brand awareness surveys that show the same rise in both places point to the season or the category. Only the gap between the two markets belongs to the campaign.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the best time to send a brand awareness survey?\", \"a\": \"Send one round in the weeks before a campaign or market launch, and another soon after it ends. For steady tracking, quarterly fits most brands. Field each round in the same weeks of the quarter, because a holiday month can shift recall more than the marketing did.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you track brand awareness survey results over time?\", \"a\": \"Hold the wording and the screener fixed, then compare each market with its own previous round. Subtract the decoy rate before reading any rise. In an Emergent-built app, every round lands in a database you own, with no cap on responses.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6accb39f13e0be4f1e5be583",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Brand Perception Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a brand perception survey?\", \"a\": \"A brand perception survey asks people how they see a brand: the words they link to it, how it rates on statements such as fair pricing, and how it compares with rivals. Run on a schedule, it shows whether that view is moving.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you create a brand perception survey?\", \"a\": \"Decide who to ask, write four to six attribute statements, and put an open first-word question ahead of them. Then add the same statements for two rivals. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> turns that outline into a working survey with its own answer table.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the purpose of brand perception surveys?\", \"a\": \"Sales figures show what people buy. Brand perception surveys show which traits buyers credit you with and where a rival is rated higher. Repeated on a schedule, they also tell you whether a pricing or service change moved the score.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions should be in a brand perception survey?\", \"a\": \"Strong brand perception survey questions cover the first word that comes to mind, agreement with attribute statements, and a comparison with named rivals. Open with one screening question so you know who is answering. Service quality for current buyers belongs in a customer satisfaction survey.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many questions should a brand perception survey include?\", \"a\": \"Count the attribute statements first, since each one repeats for every rival. Four statements across your brand and two rivals already make 12 ratings, before the screener and the first-word question. Each statement you add costs three more ratings. Keep only those a decision depends on.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a brand perception survey include competitors?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Pick the two or three that buyers weigh against you, and rate each on the statements you use for your own brand. A drop shared by every brand in the category points to the market. A drop that hits only yours points back at something you changed.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a brand perception survey template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A working brand perception survey template opens with a screening question and the open word question, then five attribute statements repeated for each rival. Describe your brand and two competitors to Emergent, and it builds that structure with every response stored in your own database.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some good brand perception survey examples?\", \"a\": \"A quarterly tracker that rates a bank against two rivals is one. A split test where each shopper sees a single package design is another. Candidates can rate a hiring process too, while staff views of the company fit an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/employee-engagement-survey'>employee engagement survey</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"How often should you send brand perception surveys?\", \"a\": \"Quarterly works for a brand that changes prices or campaigns often, and twice a year is enough in a slower category. Hold whichever cadence you choose, because a trend line needs evenly spaced points. To read a launch, add a separate wave instead of moving a regular one.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many responses should a brand perception survey collect?\", \"a\": \"Size each wave for the smallest group you plan to report on, not for the total. A wave of 400 split across four regions leaves about 100 per region, thin for a score you mean to act on. Emergent puts no cap on responses, which leaves sample size a fieldwork call, never a plan limit.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6ace1eaf7d70b298f46197d4",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Effort Score Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a customer effort score?\", \"a\": \"A customer effort score (CES) measures how easy one task was for a customer, like filing a claim or finding an answer. It comes from a single agree statement rated on seven points. Dixon, Freeman, and Toman introduced it in a 2010 Harvard Business Review article.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you create a customer effort score survey?\", \"a\": \"Choose one task to score, write the agree statement for it, and trigger the question as soon as that task is done. Then add a follow-up that only low scorers see. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> turns a plain description of all that into a working CES survey with its own answer table.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a good customer effort score?\", \"a\": \"No universal benchmark exists, because scores move with the task, the scale, and the method. Compare each task with its own past results instead. Run the same CES survey on the same task each month and treat a rising score as the good sign.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the customer effort score formula?\", \"a\": \"There are two common formulas. Average every answer: 50 answers adding up to 280 give 5.6. Or divide the answers at 5, 6, or 7 by the total, where 130 of 200 gives a score of 65.\"}, {\"q\": \"When should you send a customer effort survey?\", \"a\": \"Send it within minutes of the task it scores, while each step is still easy to recall. Answers collected days afterward say more about overall mood than about the task. A survey that fires after every finished task adds up fast, and Emergent puts no cap on responses.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between customer effort score and NPS?\", \"a\": \"CES rates how easy one task was, right after it ends. Each nps survey asks how likely a customer is to recommend you on 0 to 10, then subtracts detractors (0 to 6) from promoters (9 or 10). Use effort to fix steps and NPS to follow the relationship.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which is better, customer effort score or customer satisfaction score?\", \"a\": \"Neither replaces the other. CSAT asks how satisfied someone was, usually on five points, and counts the 4s and 5s, while effort asks how easy one task was. A customer satisfaction survey can carry the effort question in the same send.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a customer effort score survey template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A customer effort score survey template needs the agree statement and a follow-up shown only after a low answer. Add fields for the task and the customer ID, and every score can be filtered later. Describe yours to Emergent and edit the result with a prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an example of a customer effort score survey question?\", \"a\": \"A typical one is an agree statement tied to a single task, such as \\\"Returning my order was easy,\\\" rated on seven points from strongly disagree to strongly agree. The question form works too: \\\"How easy was it to set up your account?\\\" on the same seven points.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the limitations of customer effort score?\", \"a\": \"It scores one task, not the whole relationship, and a single number does not say which step went wrong. Scores also move with the scale and the wording. Two surveys that differ on either rarely compare. Pair it with a short follow-up and a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/customer-experience-survey'>customer experience survey</a> for the wider view.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6acf3f2ad9386565b4a8fd4b",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"CX Survey Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a customer experience survey?\", \"a\": \"A customer experience survey asks about several points in a customer's relationship with a company, such as buying, delivery, billing and support, instead of one transaction. Each stage's answers are tied to the same customer. The result shows which stage drags the overall impression down, and for whom.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a customer experience survey?\", \"a\": \"Map each stage of the relationship and the event that closes it, such as an order picked up or a ticket resolved. Give every stage the same rating scale and one open question. Then describe that plan to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a>, and it builds the surveys, the sends, and the dashboard that compares them.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some good survey questions to measure customer experience?\", \"a\": \"Good customer experience survey questions name one stage each. Did checkout take longer than expected? Was your pickup ready at the promised time? Did your first bill match what you expected? Follow each rating with one open question, and keep the wording neutral so it does not hint at the answer you want.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some common questions used in a customer experience survey?\", \"a\": \"They fall into four kinds. Effort questions ask how easy a task was, such as placing an order. Resolution questions ask whether a problem got fixed. A loyalty question asks for a 0 to 10 rating of how likely the customer is to recommend the company. Open questions ask for the reason, and a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/customer-feedback-survey'>customer feedback survey</a> is built around that kind.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does a customer experience survey sample look like?\", \"a\": \"Here is a short one for a software subscription. After signup: how easy was setting up your account, rated 1 to 5? After the first invoice: was the amount what you were quoted? After a support ticket closes: was your problem solved? Each rating is followed by one open question about what would have made that step better.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a customer experience survey template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Many survey tools offer one, usually a fixed list of questions about a single visit or purchase. Treat it as a starting point, and cut any question that does not match a stage in your business. With Emergent, you describe your own stages instead and get a question set for each one.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free customer experience survey?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing a survey. Some survey tools cap responses on free plans or bill for each extra one. A survey built with Emergent has no response cap, and you keep every answer.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a retail customer experience survey ask?\", \"a\": \"A retail customer experience survey should follow the way people shop: finding the product, checkout, pickup or delivery, and returns. Ask one rating and one open question for each. Shoppers who buy online and collect in store need a stage of their own, because waiting at a counter is a different experience from using the website.\"}, {\"q\": \"How are customer experience surveys different from satisfaction surveys?\", \"a\": \"Customer experience surveys cover several stages of the relationship and tie each stage's answers to the same customer. A customer satisfaction survey scores one interaction, such as a delivery or a closed support ticket. The two fit together: a satisfaction score can be one stage inside the wider survey.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between a consumer survey and a customer experience survey?\", \"a\": \"A consumer survey usually samples a whole market, including people who have never bought from you, to learn habits, prices, or brand awareness. A customer experience survey goes only to your own customers, soon after they deal with you, and asks how each stage went.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6accb44a40d5b6e947b7155a",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Feedback Survey Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a customer feedback survey?\", \"a\": \"A customer feedback survey is a short questionnaire sent after one moment, like a first delivery or a support call. It collects reasons in the customer's own words, where a satisfaction survey tracks a score over time. Both kinds of customer surveys can live in one app.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a customer feedback survey?\", \"a\": \"Pick the moment you want to hear about, such as a first delivery or a closed support ticket, and what you will change based on the replies. Describe both in a prompt, and Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> drafts the questions, the send trigger, and the table that stores every reply.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you write a good customer survey?\", \"a\": \"Write each question the way a customer will read it on a phone, in neutral words. Ask \\\"How was your visit?\\\" instead of \\\"How much did you enjoy your visit?\\\", because wording and question order both shift the answers. Drop any question whose answer would not change what you do.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some good survey questions to collect customer feedback?\", \"a\": \"Good questions name one moment and leave room for a reason. Start these survey questions for customers with a rating of the delivery, then ask for the main reason behind it. Buyers who nearly left can also say what almost stopped them from ordering. To follow one score over time, a customer satisfaction survey repeats the same rating at fixed points.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are typical customer service survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Typical customer service survey questions ask whether the issue was resolved and how the agent handled it, then leave an open box for what could have gone better. If you also track a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/customer-effort-score'>customer effort score</a>, keep it in the same app so each rating sits beside its comment. A week later, send one more question: did the problem stay fixed?\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a customer feedback survey template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A post-onboarding check-in and a delivery survey are two common first drafts. Start from either one, then reword any question with a follow-up prompt instead of editing fields by hand.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should customer feedback survey software do?\", \"a\": \"Good customer feedback survey software lets you skip anyone who answered in the last month, because nobody wants a survey after every order. A customer should be able to reply straight from the email or text, with no login. With Emergent, each reply lands in a database you own, not in a survey vendor's account.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you choose customer survey tools?\", \"a\": \"Judge customer survey tools by what happens after a reply arrives. Check that an open answer can be tagged and sent to its owner, and that replies in other languages still get read. Then read the plan limits, since some plans cap responses or bill for each one past the cap. Emergent builds the survey and its routing from a prompt, and paid plans can export the code to your GitHub.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free customer feedback survey?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing the survey. Responses have no cap, and a busy month never stops collection. Add an NPS survey to the same app later if you want a loyalty score beside the comments.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a customer service survey template include?\", \"a\": \"A customer service survey template should carry the ticket number and the agent's name as hidden fields, filled in before the customer opens it. Set it to send when the ticket closes. A rule for reopened tickets keeps anyone from being surveyed twice about one problem.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6accb44a40d5b6e947b7155c",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Satisfaction Survey Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an employee satisfaction survey?\", \"a\": \"An employee satisfaction survey asks people how content they are with specific parts of their job, from pay and benefits to their manager and working conditions. Paul Spector's Job Satisfaction Survey, a research instrument, uses 36 items across nine facets, including pay and supervision, rated on a six-point agreement scale.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an employee satisfaction survey template?\", \"a\": \"Describe the workforce and the topics to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a>, and it writes an employee satisfaction survey template you can edit, free to start. Rename topics in the words people use at work, such as \\\"planning periods\\\" in a school or \\\"rotation\\\" on a hospital unit. Nobody should have to translate a question before answering it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are good employee satisfaction survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Good ones ask about one thing at a time. \\\"Rate your schedule and workload\\\" can't be read when someone likes one and not the other. Split it in two. Keep the wording neutral, too: \\\"Rate the tools you need to do your job\\\" works where \\\"How much do you love our new tools?\\\" pushes people toward yes. The one-topic rule holds for a customer satisfaction survey as well.\"}, {\"q\": \"Are employee satisfaction surveys actually anonymous?\", \"a\": \"Only when nothing stored beside an answer points back to a person. Qualtrics, for one, logs an IP address and rough location with each response unless Anonymize Responses is switched on. Timestamps can give people away as well, if a manager knows who was on shift at 2 a.m. Ask HR what is kept with each answer.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a good score on an employee satisfaction survey?\", \"a\": \"There is no universal pass mark, and outside benchmarks rarely ask your exact questions. Small groups need care: in a team of 30, one person changing their answer moves a topic by about three points, and a seven-point drop there may be two people. Trust a change that shows up across several teams or holds for two surveys running.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions should a nurse satisfaction survey include?\", \"a\": \"Ask about what a unit manager can change: staffing on a typical shift, float assignments, whether breaks get covered, mandatory overtime, and backup from the charge nurse. Keep it short enough to finish on a break. With no response cap on Emergent, a large hospital system can send every nurse the same survey.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions belong on a teacher satisfaction survey?\", \"a\": \"Planning time, class sizes, backing from administrators on student behavior, duties outside teaching, and whether training days are worth the time. Open it while next year's schedules can still change. Surveys built on Emergent have no per-seat pricing: every principal can get a results login without a seat fee.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many workplace satisfaction survey questions should you ask?\", \"a\": \"Only enough to cover the topics leadership will act on, usually one or two items per topic plus one overall item. When people quit partway through, the last topics get the thinnest data. Time a pilot group and cut items until it fits a short break. Emergent can lay it out one question per screen, which reads well on a phone.\"}, {\"q\": \"How often should you send a staff satisfaction survey?\", \"a\": \"Once a year for the full survey, with a short check between rounds on the topics you promised to fix. Sending it more often than anyone can act on the results teaches people that answering changes nothing. Keep the items and their wording identical from round to round so the scores compare.\"}, {\"q\": \"How is a job satisfaction survey different from an engagement survey?\", \"a\": \"A job satisfaction survey asks whether the job meets people's needs, while an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/employee-engagement-survey'>employee engagement survey</a> asks how committed they are and how much extra effort they give. A team can be content and still do the minimum, or stretched thin and still committed, and the two surveys will disagree about it.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6ace1dd9b328edb4af06e8af",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Pulse Survey Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a pulse survey?\", \"a\": \"A pulse survey asks the same people a few fixed questions on a set cycle, often every week or two. Each round takes a couple of minutes, and comparing rounds shows whether a team's answers are climbing or sliding. The US Census Bureau also runs a Household Pulse Survey, started in April 2020.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you build an employee pulse survey?\", \"a\": \"Describe to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> who answers and how often. It drafts the questions and a results view split by team, and it is free to start. Send round one to a single team as a trial before the rest of the company sees it.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you provide an example of a pulse survey question?\", \"a\": \"\\\"My workload is manageable this week,\\\" rated on a 1-5 agreement scale, is a typical one. It covers one thing and still makes sense next round. Good pulse survey questions describe a present condition the team can change, not a general feeling about the company.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free pulse survey template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent writes a pulse survey template from a few lines of description, and you can start for free. Ask for a handful of employee pulse survey questions and say who hears about a falling score. Settle the wording before round one goes out. Changing it later breaks the trend line.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a college pulse survey real?\", \"a\": \"Yes. College Pulse is an online survey and analytics company that studies US undergraduates through its own student panel. It has no connection to the pulse surveys an employer sends its staff, which share only the name.\"}, {\"q\": \"How often should you run employee pulse surveys?\", \"a\": \"Weekly or every other week suits a set of about five statements, and a monthly round can carry more. Match the cadence to how fast you can act on what comes back. If a team needs two weeks to discuss results, a weekly round outruns it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is another name for a pulse survey?\", \"a\": \"Pulse check is the name you hear most, and some teams say check-in survey or micro-survey. All three mean the same format: the same handful of questions repeated on a schedule and read as a trend, not as one result. The format works with customers too, as a two-question monthly check beside a quarterly customer satisfaction survey.\"}, {\"q\": \"Are pulse surveys anonymous?\", \"a\": \"Some are, and others are confidential, which is a different promise. A confidential pulse knows who answered and can send reminders, but it hides any group below a minimum number of answers. An anonymous pulse stores no identity at all, which rules out reminders and team splits.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should employee pulse survey software do?\", \"a\": \"It should send each round on schedule and nudge only those still missing. It should also hide small groups and chart each team against its own history. Ask where the data lives, and whether you can export it if you change tools later. On Emergent the answers land in a database you own, and no cap limits how many come in.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does an employee engagement pulse survey differ from an annual one?\", \"a\": \"An annual <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/employee-engagement-survey'>employee engagement survey</a> asks dozens of items once a year to find what drives commitment. An employee engagement pulse survey repeats a handful of those core items between annual rounds. It shows whether the actions managers took are moving the score.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     }
    ]
   }
